    ("n0218", "Harlow Street Viaduct to shut for a rebuild", "The span carrying Route 9 over the Calder River will be closed to all vehicles from December 1 while crews replace its deck and bearings. Engineers expect the work to take eleven months, and the state has not yet named a detour for trucks. Buses will cross by way of the Mill Road overpass.", "Is the elevated roadway over the waterway going to be off limits to motorists for most of a year?", "para"),
    ("n0291", "Merrow Pier footbridge reopens after cable repairs", "The Merrow Pier footbridge reopened on Friday afternoon, nine days after inspectors found corroded suspension cables on its east side. Harbor officials said the replacement cables were rated for twice the load and that the lights along the deck had also been rewired.", "What happened at the Merrow Pier footbridge?", "exact"),
    ("n0102", "Senate passes Tidewater Appropriations Act 61-38", "The Senate approved the Tidewater Appropriations Act by 61 votes to 38 late Tuesday, sending the $14 billion measure for harbor dredging, levees and flood pumps to the House. Eight members of the minority party voted yes after an amendment protected inland counties from a new fee.", "How did the Senate vote on the Tidewater Appropriations Act?", "exact"),
    ("n0229", "Rooftop solar credit falls four votes short", "The upper chamber rejected a proposal to extend tax credits for rooftop solar panels on Thursday, falling four votes short of the sixty needed to end debate. Backers said they would try again after the holiday recess, while opponents called the credits a giveaway to installers.", "Did lawmakers in the upper house keep the incentives for home photovoltaic installations?", "para"),
    ("n0013", "Aldersgate Silicon pauses work on its Ohio fab", "Aldersgate Silicon told investors it has halted construction of its planned factory near Dayton, Ohio, citing delays in delivery of lithography tools and a weaker outlook for memory prices. About 1,200 construction jobs are affected. The company kept its capital budget for Arizona unchanged.", "Why did Aldersgate Silicon stop building its Ohio factory?", "exact"),
    ("n0118", "Veridian Micro cuts 900 jobs as demand cools", "Veridian Micro, which designs accelerator processors for data centers, will lay off 900 workers, nearly one in eight of its employees, after orders from its largest cloud customers slowed. The company said it still expects to ship its next-generation design in the spring.", "Which company that makes computing hardware for server farms is dismissing roughly an eighth of its staff?", "para"),
    ("n0143", "Freezing drizzle glazes roads across the Upper Valley", "A film of ice formed on roads, bridges and power lines across the Upper Valley overnight. Nineteen school districts closed or opened late, and two sections of the interstate were shut for several hours after a chain of collisions. Temperatures were forecast to rise above freezing by midday.", "Why are children staying home in the northern river valley this morning?", "para"),
    ("n0176", "Mercy General opens a 40-bed psychiatric wing", "Mercy General Hospital opened a new 40-bed psychiatric wing on Monday, the first expansion of mental health beds in the county in two decades. The wing includes a youth unit and a crisis stabilization room, and it will be staffed by 62 new nurses and counselors.", "When did Mercy General Hospital open the new wing?", "exact"),
    ("n0056", "Pell County outbreak reaches 27 cases", "Public health officials in Pell County said 27 people have now been infected in an outbreak that began when an unvaccinated child attended a church summer camp. Seventeen of the patients are under ten. Free vaccination clinics will run at three fire stations this weekend.", "How many people in the rural district have caught the contagious rash illness?", "para"),
    ("n0137", "Council lets homeowners add backyard cottages", "The city council voted 7 to 2 to allow homeowners in every residential zone to build a detached unit of up to 800 square feet behind their houses. The measure waives parking requirements near transit lines. Opponents worried about shade, noise and the loss of tree cover.", "Can residents put a small second dwelling behind their houses now?", "para"),
    ("n0246", "Gannet Point wind farm starts delivering power", "The Gannet Point wind farm began feeding 220 megawatts into the regional grid on Wednesday, enough for roughly 150,000 homes. The 62 turbines stand on a headland and offshore shoal, and the developer said a second phase of 90 megawatts would follow next summer.", "How much power does the Gannet Point wind farm supply?", "exact"),
    ("n0261", "Regulators approve a 6 percent electricity rate increase", "State utility regulators approved a 6 percent increase in residential electricity rates that takes effect in January, adding about $9 to the typical monthly bill. The utility argued the money is needed to bury lines and replace aging substations. Consumer advocates had asked for 3 percent.", "Will my monthly power charges go up after the new year?", "para"),
    ("n0276", "Lakemont water suit thrown out", "Judge Ibarra-Whitfield dismissed the Lakemont water contamination lawsuit on Monday, ruling that residents had not shown the tannery's discharge was the cause of elevated lead in their taps. Lawyers for the plaintiffs said they would appeal.", "What did Judge Ibarra-Whitfield rule?", "exact"),
    ("n0055", "Jury convicts former county treasurer", "A jury found Dale Pruitt, the county's former treasurer, guilty of taking $412,000 from the fund set aside for road repairs and covering it with falsified ledgers. He faces up to fifteen years in prison. Sentencing is set for January.", "Was the ex-official who took money meant for highways found guilty?", "para"),
