    ("n0121", "New world best in the 26.2 miles", "A 24-year-old runner from Eldoret cut 41 seconds from the world best for the distance, finishing the course along the Tagus river in 2 hours, 0 minutes and 18 seconds. Pacemakers dropped out at the 30-kilometre mark and she ran the last stretch alone.", "Did anyone set a new fastest time for the long road race in Portugal's capital?", "para"),
    ("n0138", "Rocky world found around a dim neighbor star", "Astronomers reported an Earth-sized rocky planet circling a faint red dwarf only 14 light-years away. It sits in the zone where liquid water could exist on the surface, though the star's flares may have stripped its air. The team will look for an atmosphere with the next space telescope.", "Has anyone found a possibly habitable world close to our solar system?", "para"),
    ("n0089", "Kestrel-4 touches down near lunar south pole", "The Kestrel-4 lander touched down on a ridge near the Moon's south pole on Sunday, about 600 metres from its target. The craft is tilted by eight degrees but its solar array and radio are working. It carries a drill that will sample ice-bearing soil during the two-week lunar day.", "Where did Kestrel-4 land?", "exact"),
    ("n0094", "Teachers authorize a walkout over crowded rooms", "Instructors in the Brannock school district voted 91 percent in favor of a strike if talks fail by December 5. They want caps on class sizes, which reach 38 in some middle school rooms, and a 7 percent raise. The district offered 3 percent and a hiring freeze review.", "Are educators in the eastern-county district threatening to stop teaching over packed classrooms?", "para"),
